{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new functions and refactors existing ones to improve usability and consistency. It also updates type checking logic and removes legacy Python 2 support, ensuring the library is modern and robust.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The public API must expose a function named `apply` that accepts an iterable of arguments and applies them to a callable. Additionally, `identity` and `thread_first` must be available as public names."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The release must provide a `pipe` function that takes a value and a series of functions, applying each function in sequence. It must also expose `compose_left` for left-to-right composition, alongside the existing `compose` function."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "A new function named `peekn` must be exposed publicly, allowing inspection of multiple items from an iterator without consuming them. The existing `peek` function must remain available as a public name."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The `fold` function must continue to support parallel execution by accepting a worker pool or process group argument. Its behavior regarding the combination of results using a specified operator must remain consistent with previous versions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "Any internal breakpoint signals or debugging hooks must maintain their current signature and behavior, ensuring no regression in debugging capabilities."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "text": "The `merge` and `merge_with` functions must accept any object implementing the `Mapping` abstract base class, not just standard dictionaries. This allows these functions to work with custom mapping types that adhere to the Mapping interface."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "The library must remove all Python 2 specific code paths and dependencies, targeting only Python 3 environments. Public names such as `curry`, `Compose`, `excepts`, and others listed must remain accessible and functional under this constraint."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31",
      "text": "The `get_config_from_root` function must emit improved warnings when configuration issues are detected, providing clearer diagnostic information. These warnings should follow standard Python warning categories and formats."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names are correctly exported and documented. Verify that the removal of Python 2 support does not break compatibility with supported Python 3 versions."
}
